 "text": "Court Offices | Miami County, IN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nServices\nResidents\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nCourt Offices\nCourt Offices\n9\n1\n1\n2\nCircuit Court\nLearn more about the Miami Circuit Court. The Honorable Timothy P. Spahr is the Judge of the Court.\nClerk of Courts\nThe Clerk's Office assists the Miami County Court Judges in the execution of their judicial duties by preparing, recording, and maintaining court documents.\nCommunity Corrections\nOur vision is that we will be a recognized and respected leader in our community by continuing to make a positive impact on those we serve.\nCourt Appointed Special Advocates (CASA)\nThe CASA program began in 1977 in Seattle when a judge envisioned using trained community volunteers to represent the best interest of abused and neglected children in court.\nMiami County Courts\nSee information about the different Miami County courts.\nOther Court Resources\nSee the other Miami County court resources.\nProbation\nThe Miami County Probation Department serves the Miami Circuit and Superior Courts through the preparation of pre-sentence investigation reports, preliminary investigation reports and the supervision of misdemeanor, felony and juvenile offenders.\nProsecutor\nThe Prosecutor is the people’s lawyer in the criminal justice system. He represents the interests of all of the citizens of Miami County and the State of Indiana against perpetrators of crime.\nPublic Defender\nGet information about the Office of the Public Defender.\nSuperior Court I\nGet information relating to the Honorable David Grund's Superior Court I of Miami County.\nSuperior Court II\nFind information about the Honorable Jacob D Winkler's Superior Court II of Miami County.\nVictim's Advocate\nThe Victim Advocate is responsible for assisting victims of crime as they navigate the judicial system, providing a line of communication between the Prosecutor and the victim.\nCircuit Court\nClerk of Courts\nCommunity Corrections\nCourt Appointed Special Advocates (CASA)\nMiami County Courts\nOther Court Resources\nProbation\nProsecutor\nPublic Defender\nSuperior Court I\nSuperior Court II\nVictim's Advocate\nFacebook\nContact Us\nMiami County Courthouse\n25 N Broadway\nPeru, IN 46970\nPhone Directory\nHours\nQuick Links\nBid Postings\nMiami County Officials\nElection Resources\nADA Information\nCourt Resources\nLegal Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nQuick Links\nSite Map\nHome\nAccessibility\nPrivacy\nCopyright Notices\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nEnable Google Translate\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nFacebook\nTwitter\nPinterest\nDelicious\nBlogger\nLinkedIn\nHome\nMy Account\nPrinter Friendly\nEmail Page\nContact Us\nRSS\nSite Map\nTranslate Page\nNotifications\nDocuments\nClose ×",
